From 0132b4732269f26be3229e8f03202623e4ec1ffb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tonystark101-debug
 <61789569+tonystark101-debug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:42:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dxa: coalesce tiled scatter writes in the RTL to match
 SimX

The DXA SMEM writer drains Flat/BlockMajor scatter one element per beat, so
a 64-byte line of fp16 B turns into 32 LMEM writes although each beat can
write a whole SMEM word under byte enables. On sgemm_tcu_wg_dxa that writer
is the bottleneck (tensor unit busy ~4%).

With VX_CFG_DXA_SCATTER_COALESCE, VX_dxa_smem_wr drains the run of
consecutive elements that land in the current SMEM word: the window at the
read pointer is spread to the layout's power-of-two step and shifted to the
first element's in-word offset, under a byte mask. Runs are regular
(BlockMajor: after a CL's first beat every beat fills a word; Flat: one
n-block per beat), so the beat size is min(level, cap) with cap registered
at CL load, which keeps the drain's control cone at the reference depth.

SimX now follows the RTL's rule: tiled runs end at the SMEM word (Flat also
at the n-block end), and K-major keeps one element per beat. The option is
declared in VX_config.toml, off by default. dxa.yaml gains functional
simx/rtlsim cases for BlockMajor, Flat and multicast, plus a model_parity
case.

rtlsim, sgemm_tcu_wg_dxa NT32/NW8 fp16 64x64x128: 13877 -> 8054 cycles,
LMEM writes 9216 -> 2048; SimX 8137 (1.0%). Beacon dxa (flag on vs master):
depth 15 -> 15, LUT 10686 -> 12668, p_fmax 298.6 -> 282.3 MHz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 VX_config.toml               |   3 +
 ci/testcases/dxa.yaml        |  39 +++++++++++++
 hw/rtl/dxa/VX_dxa_smem_wr.sv | 109 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 sim/simx/dxa/dxa_core.cpp    |  35 ++++++++---
 4 files changed, 178 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/VX_config.toml b/VX_config.toml
index 6e059d3..ab08d49 100644
--- a/VX_config.toml
+++ b/VX_config.toml
@@ -432,6 +432,9 @@ VX_CFG_NUM_DXA_CORES = "expr: max(1, up($VX_CFG_NUM_CORES / 8))"
 VX_CFG_DXA_MEM_PORTS = "expr: min($VX_CFG_NUM_DXA_CORES, up($VX_CFG_NUM_CORES / $VX_CFG_SOCKET_SIZE) * $VX_CFG_L1_MEM_PORTS)"
 VX_CFG_DXA_QUEUE_SIZE = 16
 VX_CFG_DXA_MAX_INFLIGHT = 8
+# Tiled (Flat/BlockMajor) scatter writes the run of elements that share an
+# LMEM word in one beat instead of one element per beat.
